  nonce: 62b1  # 62b1
  message: "Satisfied on dev 38f6c90533. Fixed by 481db32997 (stable_id F1): the 'function' handler emits one symbol per name per declaration block, from its first equation; the 'signature' handler emits only when nothing in the block implements the name (_has_equations). Behavioral evidence, filed repro re-run: Main.purs with 'foo :: Int -> Int' then 'foo x = x + 1' -> analyze_purescript yields exactly one function symbol Main.foo (4-4, signature 'Int -> Int'); the reversed order (equation then signature) also yields one symbol (3-3, same signature). Gaps left open: no regression test covers either order (the filed fix asked for both), and the comment at tests/test_purescript.py:261-264 still describes the dual emit as pre-existing."  # 62b1
